## Objection handling

### Business persona (Head of Fraud Ops / CRO)
| Objection | Response |
|---|---|
| "Synthetic data. Why should I believe the uplift?" | "You shouldn't, yet. That's why the business case uses *rates* measured on a hold-out and applies them to UK Finance and PSR baselines, not synthetic totals. The pilot re-measures on your data before anything touches a customer." |
| "My team can't absorb more alerts." | "They don't have to. The comparison is at the *same* number of holds. If you prefer, the model matches today's catch with {{K_MATCH}} holds instead of {{RULES_ALERTS}}, which is {{ALERT_REDUCTION}}% fewer." |
| "Complaints: what if we block a genuine payment?" | "Genuine holds per scam fall from {{FP_RULES}} to {{FP_MODEL}}. Every hold has plain-English reasons, and the GenAI customer message is drafted for an analyst to approve." |
| "What about vulnerable customers?" | "Vulnerability is a feature *and* a queue attribute. The case note flags it, and impersonation scripts are written for older and vulnerable customers." |
| "How fast to value?" | "Six weeks to a signed-off business case; the platform pieces already exist in your Databricks estate." |
| "How does this compare with buying a vendor scam-score?" | "Vendor scores are a useful *feature*. We can ingest them into this pipeline. What they don't give you is your own claims labels, your own analyst feedback loop and one governed view across fraud, finance and conduct." |

### Technical persona (Fraud Engineering / Architecture)
| Objection | Response |
|---|---|
| "Training/serving skew: the app rebuilds features." | "Correct, it's the prototype trade-off. `backend.build_features` mirrors the gold SQL one-to-one. In production we'd move to UC Feature Engineering with online feature serving (Lakebase-backed) so batch and online read one definition." |
| "Real-time latency budget for Faster Payments?" | "Measured in the evidence: Lakebase point lookups p50 {{PG_P50}} ms for three queries; Model Serving round-trip is in the run log. Scale-to-zero is off in production during banking hours." |
| "Why Lakebase and not just the warehouse?" | "The queue and checks are single-row reads and *transactional* writes (decision + status in one commit). A warehouse is built for scans. Lakebase gives Postgres semantics inside the same governance, and synced tables / Lakehouse Sync remove the ETL in both directions." |
| "Label leakage / time travel?" | "All window features look strictly backwards (`RANGE … 1 PRECEDING`). The split is by time, and labels come only from claims, which arrive late. The last 10 days are treated as label-immature and excluded from evaluation." |
| "Model risk / SS1/23?" | "UC model registry with aliases, evaluation tables, lineage from raw file to score, inference tables for monitoring. Champion/challenger is an alias switch." |
| "PII and the LLM?" | "Masks are applied in Unity Catalog *before* data reaches the LLM, Genie or Lakebase. The LLM sees masked names and behavioural features only, via the Foundation Model API inside the Databricks boundary." |
| "How does it scale to 190M payments a year?" | "Serverless pipeline with Photon; the gold windows are partitioned by customer/payee. Real-time scoring is stateless behind an autoscaling endpoint, and Lakebase autoscales 0.5–32 CU." |
| "GenAI hallucination in case notes?" | "The prompt only contains structured facts, the output is schema-constrained JSON, and the recommended action is advisory. The next step is MLflow evaluation with Guidelines judges on a labelled set." |

